#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Stateful fake `curl` for the Authentik API (issue #165 test harness).

Copied into a test's `bin/` directory (never imported). Models just enough of Authentik's
admin API for the evaluator install scripts: the shared API token check, groups, users,
recovery links, WebAuthn devices, user deletion, and an "unreachable" switch.

State lives in a JSON file named by $PS_TEST_CURL_STATE (created on first use). Every call
appends its argv and resolved URL to $PS_TEST_CURL_LOG. The stdin config (`--config -`) carries
the bearer token and is NEVER logged, so a test can prove a secret never reaches argv or logs.

State keys (all optional, tests seed them):
  token             the only bearer token the fake accepts (default "test-token")
  unreachable       true -> exit 7 (connection refused) for every call
  token_reject_status  HTTP status for a non-matching token (default 403, the recorded real value)
  recovery_flow     true -> recovery links work; false -> 400 "No recovery flow set."
  token_user_pk     pk of the user `GET /core/users/me/` reports for the token (default: the
                    recorded akadmin, pk 4); null -> the response carries no pk
  users             {pk: {"pk", "username", "email", "type", "groups", "is_active"}}
  devices           {pk: [{"pk": ..., "name": ..., "type": ...}]}  authenticator devices per
                    user pk; `type` is the device's `meta_model_name` (default: WebAuthn). A
                    device pk is unique only within its type, as in Authentik.
  sessions          {uuid: {"user": pk}}  authenticated sessions
  access_tokens / refresh_tokens  {pk: {"user": pk}}  OAuth2 tokens
  core_tokens       {identifier: {"user": pk, "intent": ...}}  `/core/tokens/` rows (api,
                    app_password, recovery, ...); a recovery link adds a `recovery` row
  ignore_user_filters  list of listings that ignore even their working per-user filter
                    ("devices": `admin/all/`; "sessions"; "oauth"; "core_tokens"), standing in
                    for an Authentik version whose filter stopped working
  stuck_next_page   every paginated list reports this `next` page number (a broken pagination)
  fail_on           {"<METHOD> <path prefix under /api/v3>": status}: that request answers
                    `status` with {"detail": "fake failure"} and changes nothing
  on_request        {"<METHOD> <path prefix under /api/v3>": {<state key>: rows}}: after the
                    first successful matching request, the rows are added to that state key
                    (lists per user pk are extended, other entries set) and the trigger is
                    removed; stands for a credential created while a script runs
  next_pk           counter for new users
  blueprints        list of blueprint instances (default: the bundled and local-TLS ones)
  blueprint_list_empty_calls  the first N blueprint lists return no instance (fresh install)
  ingress_status_endpoint_status  HTTP status of /status through the ingress on port 30443
                    (default 200)
  ingress_livez_status  HTTP status of /livez through the ingress (default 404: an in-cluster
                    probe the ingress does not route)
  ingress_issuer    the issuer the discovery document reports through the ingress (default: the
                    requested one)
  ingress_mcp_status  HTTP status of /mcp/ without a bearer token through the ingress (default 401)
  ingress_open_paths  request paths the ingress wrongly answers 200 (default none); every other
                    path outside the allowlist answers `ingress_denied_status` (default 404)
  ingress_denied_status  HTTP status of a path outside the allowlist (default 404)
  ingress_redirect_location  the Location of the allowlisted redirecting flow path (default: the
                    requested authority under /auth/)

Response shapes are RECORDED from a real Authentik 2026.8.3 (LC1b tracer, issue #165) and live
in `authentik/*.json` next to this file (secrets and per-run values sanitised). The fake loads
them from `$PS_TEST_CURL_FIXTURES` or, by default, the `authentik/` directory beside this script;
a test that copies the fake into a temp `bin/` must copy that directory too or set the variable.
Real-Authentik behaviours the recording revealed and this fake reproduces on purpose:
  - an invalid API token is HTTP 403 (not 401) with {"detail": "Token invalid/expired"};
  - `POST /core/users/` requires `name`;
  - every per-type device list (`GET /authenticators/admin/<type>/`) IGNORES a `user` or
    `user__username` query and lists every user's devices of that type; the per-user filter is
    `GET /authenticators/admin/all/?user=<pk>` (a bare JSON array of every type);
  - a device is retrieved and deleted at its type's path (`<type path><pk>/`); the retrieve
    embeds `user.pk`, except the endpoint device (no user) and the Apple Independent Secure
    Enclave (`user` is a bare pk); a repeated DELETE is 404;
  - a recovery link is built from the request's own scheme and authority;
  - sessions and core tokens filter only by `user__username` and IGNORE `user`; the OAuth2
    access/refresh token lists filter only by `user` (an unknown pk is a 400) and IGNORE
    `user__username`;
  - paginated lists take `page_size` (default 20, capped at 100) and `page`; `pagination.next`
    is the next page number or 0, and a page past the end is a 404 "Invalid page.".
"""

